# The demo quest, "Apples for the Arena" (LOT-120): its four dialogues and its journal.
dialogue.mere.speaker = The mother
dialogue.mere.appel = You! You look like someone who can fight. My son took three apples from my stall — my own apples! — and an Ironhand guard is taking him to the Arena of Fate for "theft on the public way". He is ten. Catch them on the forecourt, I beg you.
dialogue.mere.appel.accepter = I will bring him back. Which way did they go?
dialogue.mere.appel.refuser = None of my business.
dialogue.mere.merci = Down Stravian Avenue, to the east: the guard took him that way, towards the arena forecourt. Bring him back to me.
dialogue.mere.attente = Hurry… they are on the Arenarea forecourt, down the avenue to the east. I dare not leave the stall.
dialogue.mere.retrouvailles = He is here! He is here… I do not know how you did it, and I do not want to know. Take some apples. Take them all.
dialogue.mere.retrouvailles.sourire = Keep them. He will be hungry.
dialogue.garde.speaker = The Ironhand guard
dialogue.garde.halte = Move along. This boy stole from a market stall, and the Arena of Fate judges thieves like anyone else. The sand will decide.
dialogue.garde.halte.convaincre = Three apples, from his own mother's stall. Let him go.
dialogue.garde.halte.endosser = I told him to take them. Take me in his place.
dialogue.garde.halte.partir = Do your job.
dialogue.garde.adieu = …His own mother? Damned market. Off you go, boy, and don't let me see you again. You, stranger: I never saw you.
dialogue.garde.refus = No. The law does not sort between stalls. Anything else to tell me, or will you move along?
dialogue.garde.refus.endosser = I told him to take them. Take me in his place.
dialogue.garde.refus.partir = Nothing. I'm moving along.
dialogue.garde.refus-encore = I already told you: no. Anything else?
dialogue.garde.refus-encore.endosser = I told him to take them. Take me in his place.
dialogue.garde.refus-encore.partir = No. Nothing.
dialogue.garde.escorte = You? So be it. A grown man who fights, the crowd prefers that. Off you go, boy. You, follow me to the arena stairs: the convicts' changing room is below, and the door closes behind you.
dialogue.enfant.speaker = The child
dialogue.enfant.escorte = They had fallen, the apples… They were on the ground. I don't want to go into the arena.
dialogue.enfant.libre = Mum says you are a hero. I say you are weird. Thanks anyway.
dialogue.maitre-arene.speaker = The arena master
dialogue.maitre-arene.defi = The convict from the market. The crowd wants a judgement, not an execution: fight well, and it will give you your freedom. Fight badly… the sand keeps everything. Ready?
dialogue.maitre-arene.defi.combattre = Let your fighter loose.
dialogue.maitre-arene.defi.attendre = One more moment.
quest.pommes.title = Apples for the Arena
quest.pommes.acceptee = Catch up with the guard and the child on the Arenarea forecourt, down Stravian Avenue.
quest.pommes.persuasion-echouee = The guard refused to release the child. What remains is to take the blame.
quest.pommes.condamne = Convicted in the child's place: go down to the changing room, up onto the sand, and fight.
quest.pommes.victoire = The arena fighter has fallen: the crowd has given its judgement.
quest.pommes.enfant-libere = The child is free. Bring him back to his mother, on the stall square of Martpart.
quest.pommes.rendue = The child is back with his mother.
